RAWPANEL.CONF(5)

# NAME

rawpanel.conf - rawpanel configuration

# DESCRIPTION

The file uses libconfig syntax. It contains only panel-local presentation,
status, tray, and pointer-interaction policy.

In normal mode rawpanel starts with compiled defaults, applies
_${SYSCONFDIR}/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_ (normally
_/etc/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_) when present, then applies the XDG user file.
Later scalar settings override earlier values; *buttons* replaces the complete
button list when present, while named status sources overlay the source with the
same identifier. With *rawpanel -c FILE*, system and user discovery are skipped
and exactly _FILE_ is applied to compiled defaults.

The schema is fail-closed. Unknown settings and settings with the wrong type are
errors.

# PANEL

*panel* is a group. Supported members are *font*, *position* (*top* or
*bottom*), *height*, *padding*, *item\_spacing*, *section\_spacing*,
*cell\_margin*, *indicator\_size*, *tags* (*occupied* or *all*), and *colors*.

*font* is a Fontconfig/Xft pattern. The matched face is the primary panel font.
When it lacks a Unicode character, rawpanel asks Fontconfig for a scalable
monochrome fallback face, caches it, and vertically centers that face inside the
same panel text line. Color-font fallback is intentionally excluded because Xft
cannot reliably rasterize every color-font format, including COLR v1. Install a
monochrome outline font covering the desired characters when the primary face
does not provide them.

*colors* contains the groups *normal*, *selected*, *floating*, *urgent*, and
*error*. Each color group accepts *border*, *foreground*, and *background*.

# SYSTRAY

*systray* accepts *enabled*, *spacing*, and *icon\_size*.

# STATUS

*status* accepts *enabled*, *separator*, and *sources*. Sources are named and
use the native providers *alsa*, *battery*, *clock*, *cpu*, *exec*,
*filesystem*, *memory*, and *network*.

# BUTTONS

*buttons* is a list of groups with *target*, *button*, *action*, and optional
*modifiers*. Targets are *tag\_bar*, *layout*, *title*, and *status*.

Window-manager actions use rawm's published command membrane. Native volume
actions are *volume\_up*, *volume\_down*, and *volume\_mute*. *exec* requires an
*argv* vector and is deliberately local to the clicked panel surface.

Status bindings may add *id*. Tag actions take the tag under the pointer unless
an explicit *tag* is supplied. Directional actions may use *number*. Layout
actions may use *layout*.

# FILES

_${SYSCONFDIR}/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_
	System configuration, normally _/etc/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_.

_$XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_
	User override when *XDG_CONFIG_HOME* is absolute.

_$HOME/.config/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_
	User override otherwise.

# SEE ALSO

*rawpanel*(1), *rawm*(1)
